{
  "1": [
    {
      "text": "The first silver coins were minted in",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.17
    },
    {
      "text": "Lydia in what is now western Turkey",
      "startSec": 2.17,
      "endSec": 4.13
    },
    {
      "text": "around 600 BC.",
      "startSec": 4.13,
      "endSec": 5.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Silver was money before the Roman",
      "startSec": 5.6,
      "endSec": 7.12
    },
    {
      "text": "Empire, before most written languages,",
      "startSec": 7.12,
      "endSec": 9.26
    },
    {
      "text": "and it held its value through all of it",
      "startSec": 9.26,
      "endSec": 10.8
    },
    {
      "text": ".",
      "startSec": 10.8,
      "endSec": 10.8
    }
  ],
  "2": [
    {
      "text": "At its peak, the Roman denarius was 95%",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.82
    },
    {
      "text": "silver. By 268 AD, it had been debased",
      "startSec": 2.82,
      "endSec": 5.28
    },
    {
      "text": "to just 5%.",
      "startSec": 5.28,
      "endSec": 6.4
    },
    {
      "text": "Inflation followed. The economy",
      "startSec": 6.4,
      "endSec": 7.79
    },
    {
      "text": "fractured. The empire began to collapse",
      "startSec": 7.79,
      "endSec": 9.43
    },
    {
      "text": ". The pattern was not unique to Rome.",
      "startSec": 9.43,
      "endSec": 11.44
    }
  ],
  "3": [
    {
      "text": "Every USA dime, quarter, and dollar",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.06
    },
    {
      "text": "minted before 1965 was 90% real silver.",
      "startSec": 2.06,
      "endSec": 5.44
    },
    {
      "text": "In 1965, the USA removed silver from",
      "startSec": 5.44,
      "endSec": 8.05
    },
    {
      "text": "all circulating coins.",
      "startSec": 8.05,
      "endSec": 9.36
    },
    {
      "text": "Those old coins are worth far more than",
      "startSec": 9.36,
      "endSec": 11.03
    },
    {
      "text": "face value today.",
      "startSec": 11.03,
      "endSec": 12
    }
  ],
  "4": [
    {
      "text": "The full post covers every era from",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.96
    },
    {
      "text": "ancient Lydia to 1965 and what it means",
      "startSec": 1.96,
      "endSec": 4.39
    },
    {
      "text": "for silver buyers today.",
      "startSec": 4.39,
      "endSec": 5.84
    }
  ]
}